From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:33:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: log channel-set errors at warning level

The default message priority filters MSG_DEBUG while retaining warnings.
Log only rejected channel operations, with the interface and nl80211
command so the kernel error can be identified on affected radios.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -6361,8 +6361,11 @@
 		nl80211_link_set_freq(bss, freq->link_id, freq->freq);
 		return 0;
 	}
-	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "nl80211: Failed to set channel (freq=%d): "
-		   "%d (%s)", freq->freq, ret, strerror(-ret));
+	wpa_printf(MSG_WARNING,
+		   "nl80211: Failed to set channel on %s via %s "
+		   "(freq=%d): %d (%s)", bss->ifname,
+		   set_chan ? "SET_CHANNEL" : "SET_WIPHY",
+		   freq->freq, ret, strerror(-ret));
 	return -1;
 }
 
